  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questions:
  - description: Forces are pushes and pulls. If the forces are balanced, nothing
      moves (like a tied tug-of-war). If they are unbalanced, something changes speed
      or direction.
    trueAnswer: Balanced
    answers:
    - Balanced
    - Imbalanced
    - Rope is too heavy
  - description: What cause the apple to fall off a tree towards the ground?
    trueAnswer: Gravity
    answers:
    - Wind
    - Gravity
  - description: You and two friends push a stalled tricycle. It finally starts moving
      forward. Why?
    trueAnswer: Balanced forces
    answers:
    - The tricycle got lighter magically
    - Balanced forces
    - No force was applied
  - description: You drop a crumpled paper and a flat sheet. Why does the flat one
      fall slower?
    trueAnswer: Gravity and air resistance
    answers:
    - Only gravity pulls
    - Gravity and air resistance
    - No forces
    - The paper is lazy
  - description: A tennis ball hits a wall. Which of these statements is true?
    trueAnswer: Bounces Back
    answers:
    - Bounces Back
    - It sticks to the wall
  - description: When does the force of gravity exist?
    trueAnswer: Apply strength
    answers:
    - Apply strength
    - Apply telekinesis
    - Apply black magic
